  "summary": "",
  "description": "Surface app feedback to the user via a lightweight toast/notification surface, with two immediate hooks: (1) notify when a keybinding/action is blocked by the interaction policy (today silently discarded with only a debug log — AGENTS §Interaction Policy), and (2) notify on config reload outcome (success vs warning when the reload failed, replacing the `eprintln!`-only path in `main.rs::reload_config`).\n\nArchitecture: the `heca-grid-ui` `Toast` widget (`heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/toast.rs`, `toast_stack.rs`) already exists but is NOT mounted in the app today — no toast host is wired (`grep ToastStack heca/src/` = empty). So this phase must first wire a toast host (a retained overlay band or chrome region that owns a `ToastStack` and exposes a `push_toast` API reachable from handlers), then add the two hooks. The full notification architecture lives in the separate Notification System feature (fc19894f); this phase delivers a minimal, reusable toast surface and the two QoL hooks, not the full store/lifecycle/routing system.\n\nCode refs (verified 2026-07-09):\n- Blocked path: `heca/src/app/interaction.rs` — `route_action` (~:471) returns `RouteDecision::Block` for policy-blocked actions (arms at :427/:435/:443/:450/:458 and floating-domain blocks at :491/:501/:508); `dispatch_action`/`dispatch_intent` are the chokepoints where a blocked action is silently dropped (AGENTS: \"silently discarded — debug log\"). The notification should fire here with the blocked action's label (from `ActionCatalog`).\n- Reload path: `heca/src/main.rs:96` `HecaApp::reload_config` — error arm `eprintln!(\"[heca] reload failed: {e}\")` (:101) and success arm (continues at :108+). `heca/src/handlers.rs:2312` `handle_reload_config` just sets `pending_reload = true`; the actual reload + outcome is in `main.rs::reload_config` (called from :240 on `pending_reload`).\n- Toast widget: `heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/toast.rs`, `toast_stack.rs`; chrome refs in `heca/src/chrome/realize.rs` + `view.rs`.",
